# StarVMC/Geometry — AGML XML Detector Geometry Module Library

## Purpose

`StarVMC/Geometry/` is the AGML (A Geometry Modelling Language) XML geometry library for the STAR
experiment.  Each subdirectory holds the XML source for one detector subsystem.  The AGML build
system (`AgML`) compiles these XML files into C++ classes that are dynamically loaded by `starsim`
to construct the GEANT3/ROOT-based simulation geometry.

AGML is the successor to the legacy AGE (A Geometry Engine) `.g` source files that live in
`pams/geometry/`.  AGML reuses the same geometry descriptions but wraps them in structured XML and
generates portable C++ output; new development targets AGML exclusively.

---

## XML File Structure

### Top-level `<Document>` element

Every XML file begins with a `<Document file="...">` element whose `file` attribute records the
canonical path within the repository (used by the build system to locate the file).

### Module definition

Inside `<Document>` is a `<Module>` element that maps to a single FORTRAN/AGE module:

```xml
<Module name="TPCEGEO1" comment="is the TPC system in GSTAR">
  <Author name="David Underwood and Maxim Potekhin"/>
  <Created date="March 7, 2005"/>
  <CDE>AGECOM GCUNIT GCONST</CDE>
  <Content>TPCE,TOFC,TOFS,...</Content>
  ...
</Module>
```

| Element | Meaning |
|---------|---------|
| `name` | Uppercase FORTRAN module name (≤8 characters) |
| `comment` | Free-text description |
| `<CDE>` | STARSIM common-data-entry (CDE) blocks to include (analogous to `COMMON` or `#include`) |
| `<Content>` | List of GEANT volumes declared in this module |

### Structure definitions

Geometry parameters are grouped into named structures that map to FORTRAN `COMMON` blocks:

```xml
<Structure name="TPCG">
  <var name="version"  type="float"/>
  <var name="rmin"     type="float"/>
  <var name="rmax"     type="float"/>
  ...
</Structure>
```

These structures are populated through `<Fill>` elements in the same file or overridden at runtime
by `<Init>` elements in the corresponding `*Config.xml`.

### Block geometry

Inside the module body, `<Block>` elements define GEANT volumes (shape, material, position,
daughters).  The `AGML` language provides loop constructs, conditionals, and placement operations
that are expanded by the compiler into C++.

### Legacy verbatim import

Some early modules use a verbatim-import shim rather than a native AGML translation:

```xml
<Export language="Mortran">
  <Import file="pams/geometry/tpcegeo/tpcegeo.g" verbatim="true" />
</Export>
```

These are wrapped by a thin `<Document>` so that the AGML loader can handle them, but the body is
raw AGE FORTRAN.  The `Compat/` directory (see below) contains similar shims for modules that were
never ported.

