## Configuration System

### `*Config.xml`

Every detector subdirectory (except a few with no independent configuration, e.g. `TpcxGeo`,
`TutrGeo`) contains a `*Config.xml` file.  This file lists:

* **`<Detector>`** — the detector name and brief description.
* **`<Modules>`** — the set of XML module files that implement this detector.
* **`<Setup>`** — named configuration presets.

Example from `TpceConfig.xml`:

```xml
<Detector name="TPCE" comment="STAR Time Projection Chamber">
  <Modules>
    TpceGeo2, TpceGeo3a, TpceGeo4, TpceGeo1, TpceGeo5, TpceGeo6
  </Modules>

  <Setup name="TPCE00" onoff="on" module="TpceGeo1" simu="2">
  </Setup>

  <Setup name="TPCE31" onoff="on" module="TpceGeo3a" simu="2">
    <Init struct="tpcc" var="version" value="3.1"/>
    <Init struct="tpcg" var="rmax"    value="207.77"/>
  </Setup>
  ...
</Detector>
```

### `<Setup>` attributes

| Attribute | Meaning |
|-----------|---------|
| `name` | Setup identifier used by geometry tags (e.g. `TPCE31`) |
| `onoff` | Whether the detector is active (`on`) or omitted (`off`) |
| `module` | The XML module file to load for this setup |
| `simu` | Simulation mode flag (`1` = full GEANT tracking, `2` = fast mode) |
| `top` | GEANT mother volume under which this detector is placed (if non-default) |

### `<Init>` elements

`<Init struct="..." var="..." value="..."/>` injects a parameter value into a named `<Structure>`
variable before the module's geometry code runs.  This is how the same module source implements
different detector configurations — the code branches on the structure value at runtime.

For example, `TPCE31` and `TPCE32` both use `TpceGeo3a` but set `tpcc.version` to `3.1` and
`3.2` respectively to enable different pad-row numbering.

