## Geometry Tags and `StarGeo.xml`

### `StarGeo.xml` (formerly `GeometryTags.xml`)

The top-level file `StarVMC/Geometry/StarGeo.xml` defines all named geometry configurations
(tags) that users pass to `starsim` via `DETP GEOM <tag>`.  Its default tag is `y2016`.

Each `<Geometry>` element enumerates one `<Construct>` per subsystem, referencing the subsystem
name (`sys=`) and the desired setup from its `*Config.xml` (`config=`):

```xml
<Geometry tag="y2025" comment="STAR initial production tag y2025">
  <Construct sys="cave" config="CAVE06"  />
  <Construct sys="tpce" config="TPCEv61" />
  <Construct sys="btof" config="BTOFv8"  />
  <Construct sys="epdm" config="EPDMv1"  />
  ...
</Geometry>
```

### Defined tags (y2003–y2025 + development)

`StarGeo.xml` defines over 100 geometry tags.  Production tags follow the convention `y<YYYY>[a–z]`
(e.g. `y2023b`).  Development tags use names like `dev2022`, `dev2022m`, `dev2022sm`.  Special-
purpose tags include `ftsver1`–`ftsver4` (Forward Tracking System reference geometries) and
`blackhole` (absorbs all particles for systematic studies).

Tags accumulate detector changes incrementally: `y2023b` differs from `y2023a` only in the
components where the detector configuration changed between those releases.

### AGML 2 execution model

In AGML 2 (used for tags y2014+), the tag is executed immediately as it is recognized in the
`DETP GEOM` parameter loop.  The detector modules are then constructed in the order specified by
the `<Construct>` elements.  Parameters can be overridden on the command line:

```
DETP GEOM y2023b field=-5.0
```

