## Relationship to `pams/geometry/`

`pams/geometry/` contains the original AGE `.g` source files (FORTRAN-like AGE macro language)
used by the GEANT3-based `starsim` since the late 1990s.  These are compiled by the AGE
preprocessor (`mortran`) directly into FORTRAN subroutines.

`StarVMC/Geometry/` provides the AGML XML equivalents.  For most detectors the XML is a native
reimplementation in AGML syntax; for a handful of older modules the XML is a verbatim-import shim
(see `Compat/`).  The AGML output (C++) is loaded at runtime by `AgML` and produces the same
GEANT3 geometry tree as the `pams/geometry/` source.

Development since ~2012 targets `StarVMC/Geometry/` exclusively; `pams/geometry/geometry.g` was
frozen at revision 1.297 (July 2016) and no longer receives geometry-tag updates.
